From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:38:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Confirm Piano DMA stopped before
 returning buffers

Stop submitting new addresses and verify write-master completion
against the two outstanding buffers. Check both luma and chroma on
PIX. If completion cannot be established, isolate the whole camera
IOMMU stream before allowing Videobuf2 to return or unmap buffers.
Keep buffers and the powered pipeline if isolation is not confirmed.
The same stop path runs before device removal and shutdown. Hold
the kexec block until DMA is safe, or until reset after isolation.

Use the VFE 980 write-master completion registers to confirm the
existing Piano shutdown policy. Retain both NV12 plane checks.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/vendor_qcom_opensource_camera-kernel/blob/piano-w-oss/drivers/cam_isp/isp_hw_mgr/isp_hw/vfe_hw/vfe17x/cam_tfe980.h
Assisted-by: LLM

Keep the kexec reference until the usual stop path has made the DMA
buffers safe if the test pattern generator fails to start.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/vendor_qcom_opensource_camera-kernel/commit/ffb4f2bb56d41fc882682ece737e552c1a09ea65
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
